{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538003-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition-the-book-of-nod-deluxe-artifact-edition","id":1538003,"title":"Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition The Book of Nod Deluxe Artifact Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-02T10:28:03-07:00","id":1538003,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon6.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition The Book of Nod Deluxe Artifact Edition","content":"So, the last time I ran a <i>World of Darkness</i> campaign (with two Vampires, one Changeling, and several Mages) was back in the late 90s/early 00s, and the birth of my daughter last year means my ability to plan long campaigns is <i>extremely limited</i> for the foreseeable future. However, even I have to admit to temptation when I saw the <a href=\"https://renegadegamestudios.com/vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition-the-book-of-nod-deluxe-artifact-edition/\" target=\"_blank\"><b><i>Book of Nod Deluxe Artifact Edition</i></b></a> from Renegade Game Studio. It's exactly the kind of tactile item that adds interest and encourages engagement with the campaign on the part of the players. Even though I never ran a &quot;pure&quot; vampire campaign, as a prop it's tempting because it's just that pretty; if it was a little cheaper, I might even buy it with no plans to ever use it, just for inspiration from handling it and comparing it to the original book (which I bought new in 1995!)<br /> <br /> I have a question about it, if someone on these forums has picked it up (which, I think there's a good chance of that). I was thinking, if I did such a prop, I'd want to do it with &quot;texts&quot; that look and feel like the originals they're supposed to be. So, Old English (or whatever) language, illuminations where appropriate, vellum paper (or something that feels like vellum), etc. Are the pieces in the Artifact Edition done this way? One of the things I enjoyed with my <i>Call of Cthulhu</i> games was making props and printing them on newsprint, or otherwise making them seem like the Real Deal instead of something I cooked up in my game room in a few hours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#2980b9\"><b>ROLAND VOLZ</b></span><br /> <b>Running: </b><a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/prokopetz/144980905802/invisiblemelonmoose-prokopetz\" target=\"_blank\">1870s Mashup Hero System Home Game</a> | <b>Playing:</b> nothing\u200b<br /> <i>D&amp;D is an elf from Tolkien, a barbarian from Howard, and a mage from Vance fighting monsters from Lovecraft in a room that looks like it might have been designed by Wells and Giger.</i> - TiaNadiezja","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28542-alhazred","name":"AlHazred","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28542_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T07:46:57-07:00","id":1538359,"title":"","content":"I was expecting this item would have been more popular; the lack of response makes me think no one has picked it up! I'll probably give it a pass, then -- I don't trust the curated comments on the items page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#2980b9\"><b>ROLAND VOLZ</b></span><br /> <b>Running: </b><a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/prokopetz/144980905802/invisiblemelonmoose-prokopetz\" target=\"_blank\">1870s Mashup Hero System Home Game</a> | <b>Playing:</b> nothing\u200b<br /> <i>D&amp;D is an elf from Tolkien, a barbarian from Howard, and a mage from Vance fighting monsters from Lovecraft in a room that looks like it might have been designed by Wells and Giger.</i> - TiaNadiezja","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28542-alhazred","name":"AlHazred","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28542_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T09:56:21-07:00","id":1538371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AlHazred</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538003-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition-the-book-of-nod-deluxe-artifact-edition?p=1538359#post1538359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was expecting this item would have been more popular; the lack of response makes me think no one has picked it up! I'll probably give it a pass, then -- I don't trust the curated comments on the items page.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason people didn't care is because you can buy the original version from RPGnow for like a third of the cost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/gMmSwk0dUyo\" data-code=\"gMmSwk0dUyo\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/gMmSwk0dUyo/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div>