"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T14:19:48-07:00","id":1538387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538003-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition-the-book-of-nod-deluxe-artifact-edition?p=1538371#post1538371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The reason people didn't care is because you can buy the original version from RPGnow for like a third of the cost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/gMmSwk0dUyo\" data-code=\"gMmSwk0dUyo\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/gMmSwk0dUyo/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't that. Or rather, this is a full-on prop version of the previous one. So you could, for instance, play a VtM chronicle, follow in DeLaurent's footsteps and hand players actual packets of &quot;ancient writings&quot; as they find them. It looks really, really cool. I'm enough of a prop nerd (from <i>Call of Cthulhu</i>) to wonder what sort of paper they went with to get an authentic feel of &quot;ancient writings&quot;...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#2980b9\"><b>ROLAND VOLZ</b></span><br /> <b>Running: </b><a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/prokopetz/144980905802/invisiblemelonmoose-prokopetz\" target=\"_blank\">1870s Mashup Hero System Home Game</a> | <b>Playing:</b> nothing\u200b<br /> <i>D&amp;D is an elf from Tolkien, a barbarian from Howard, and a mage from Vance fighting monsters from Lovecraft in a room that looks like it might have been designed by Wells and Giger.</i> - TiaNadiezja","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28542-alhazred","name":"AlHazred","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28542_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T14:46:41-07:00","id":1538388,"title":"","content":"I looked at it on the Renegade website and the photos made me think of the type of quality you'd get with one of those videogame-deluxe-editions. Also, Renegade isn't the place I'd go to for a fair deal anyway. You'll be paying extra no matter what considering how they're pricing their books and pdfs.<br /> <br /> I haven't looked at the pricing of creating these kinds of props on your own but I'd imagine it would be cheaper to do it that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T18:28:54-07:00","id":1538399,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think here you're probably better doing the stuff than buying it, if for no other reason, because you'll have a lot of quality control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T19:04:55-07:00","id":1538400,"title":"","content":"Fair enough! Thank you for helping me overcome the urge to get it! I suspected it wasn't going to be nice enough to justify the price tag!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#2980b9\"><b>ROLAND VOLZ</b></span><br /> <b>Running: </b><a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/prokopetz/144980905802/invisiblemelonmoose-prokopetz\" target=\"_blank\">1870s Mashup Hero System Home Game</a> | <b>Playing:</b> nothing\u200b<br /> <i>D&amp;D is an elf from Tolkien, a barbarian from Howard, and a mage from Vance fighting monsters from Lovecraft in a room that looks like it might have been designed by Wells and Giger.</i> - TiaNadiezja","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28542-alhazred","name":"AlHazred","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28542_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-27T10:07:38-08:00","id":1547275,"title":"","content":"Well, I DID buy it, when it first went on sale. And let me say, it is kind of amazing! Of course, your mileage may vary.<br /> <br /> Just a little background on this may help you, I think. The project was announced in late 2021, and then COVID infrastructure snags, shipping slowdowns, and whatnot all happened. That made for a LOT of delays and up-in-the-air nonsense. Renegade did a great job of keeping the pre-order folx in the loop as to what had happened, and they offered refunds. I kept with it, as they promised to add material and improve on what they had promised. I was very unhappy to wait almost two years for this thing to arrive, no joke. At least I was given updates. When it arrived, I was not at home, forced to live in a hotel because of some remodel work. It was an anxious couple of days before I could open the package.<br /> <br /> My initial surprise was the box alone. It isn't, like, a proper packing crate, but it IS a solid wood box with Aristotle de Laurent's name on it? I felt just breathless when I saw it. It is freakin' MASSIVE.<br /> <br /> Opening it up, I didn't quite know where to start, but let me tell you a bit about the texts.<br /> <br /> First is the journal, real leather, and all in a script that is fairly easy to read, even if old Aristotle has some odd uses of letters. This is an authentic feeling artefact, without any illustrations and with all footnotes included. <br /> <br /> Next is Ayisha's letter (as seen in the end of the <b>Book of Nod</b> that is discussed above). It is okay, and maybe my first disappointment. However...<br /> <br /> The &quot;apocryphal texts&quot; are all contained in a single leather sheath, real leather with the &quot;Book of Nod&quot; logo (the seventeen skulls motif) embossed on it. Inside are the texts, which are PRETTY sweet. There are some in Latin, one in decent Greek, and one on faux papyrus telling the tale of Set. They are not EXACTLY the artefacts that I'd make, but I tell you what, they are lovely. There is detailed attention paid to the ink colours, to the apparent styles of writing, to the spelling and the papers. I cannot say enough about how gorgeous they are. Some are texts that are printed in various Vampire: The Masquerade books (e.g. The Traditions) and some are translations of passages from the <b>Book of Nod</b>. There are some new texts, too. <br /> <br /> ...And there is more wonderful fluff in the box. The photos from Aristotle's travels are nice, but the little descriptions written on the backs just make me stupid-happy. The cards of proverbs feel like they are right out of de Laurent's collection, and the statues are just amazing. Mind you, I don't love all of it. The skull is way too big to feel authentic, and the pages of original are are overkill.<br /> <br /> Renegade Game Studios really did create something wonderful with this, and I'm not going to advocate shelling out the money for it to everyone. I WILL say that I have found it an amazing investment, and the cost (my pre-order was a little less than the retain on the Renegade site) feels like a steal. <br /> <br /> Finally, here is a link to an upboxing video: <a href=\"https://youtu.be/cvj23uheamA?si=qtZdAFqHmfe-t36A\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/cvj23uheamA?si=qtZdAFqHmfe-t36A</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-10T22:32:52-08:00","id":1547675,"title":"","content":"I bought mine on Dec. 20, 2021 when they were advertising that only 500 of them would be made. I haven't taken mine out of the box.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-19T07:38:02-07:00","id":1549442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538003-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition-the-book-of-nod-deluxe-artifact-edition?p=1547275#post1547275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I DID buy it, when it first went on sale. And let me say, it is kind of amazing! Of course, your mileage may vary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great, now I have to wrestle with acquisitiveness again! LOL<br /> <br /> That sounds like an amazing prop. Thank you very much for your review!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#2980b9\"><b>ROLAND VOLZ</b></span><br /> <b>Running: </b><a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/prokopetz/144980905802/invisiblemelonmoose-prokopetz\" target=\"_blank\">1870s Mashup Hero System Home Game</a> | <b>Playing:</b> nothing\u200b<br /> <i>D&amp;D is an elf from Tolkien, a barbarian from Howard, and a mage from Vance fighting monsters from Lovecraft in a room that looks like it might have been designed by Wells and Giger.</i> - TiaNadiezja","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28542-alhazred","name":"AlHazred","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28542_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}